{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Clear sealant feels like a plausible next purchase alongside my recent anchors and wood screws because it could help finish a home repair.",
    "Both clear sealants fit that possible maintenance need, and a single cartridge or two-pack feels manageable; I would choose one option this time."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Hose clamps, a brass fitting and metal cutting wheels require specific repair needs or compatible equipment that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Finish nails are not interchangeable with my framing nails; the nail type and tool fit matter more than both being fasteners.",
    "Medicine cups do not imply that I need a stethoscope, and twelve wastebaskets or six white sealant cartridges exceed any need I currently have.",
    "Caulk caps feel premature because I have not yet opened a cartridge that needs storing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair-supply purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any plumbing, cutting or fastening supply.",
    "An isolated medicine-cup purchase seems to have been taken as interest in medical examination equipment."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Exact dimensions, fastener type and tool compatibility matter when I choose supplies; a broadly similar purpose is not enough.",
    "Quantity, clear versus white sealant, and whether I actually have a task underway affect whether an otherwise relevant item makes sense now.",
    "My history includes separate practical needs, so one purchase should not imply that I need a whole set of related equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions partly recognize my home repair needs but stretch them into supplies whose task, compatibility or quantity does not fit what I need now."
}"}
